course: dictionary
lesson: 3710
title: A name with a story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fleming is a family name, a surname, like Smith or Jones. The capital F shows it is the name of a person, not an ordinary word. «Toby's friend says Fleming found penicillin and saved everybody in like a day.» Here Fleming is a person's name, and the words around it show which person.
explain: Read the words around a name to find out who is meant. «In 1928 Alexander Fleming noticed that a mould on a dish had killed the bacteria around it.» The first name Alexander and the year 1928 tell you exactly who, and when.
explain: Check big claims against the other sentences. Toby's friend says Fleming saved everybody in a day, but the text shows that it took many years: «it took Florey, Chain and many others until the 1940s to turn it into a medicine.» A good story is one that matches all the clues.
fact: Fleming is a surname, a family name shared by many people.
fact: «Alexander Fleming» was a Scottish scientist who discovered penicillin in 1928.
fact: Penicillin was the first widely used antibiotic, a medicine that fights germs.
fact: Alexander Fleming noticed that a mould killed bacteria on a dish, and that noticing led to penicillin.
fact: «Fleming» can also mean a person from Flanders, the Dutch-speaking north of Belgium, and Ian Fleming wrote the James Bond spy stories.
exercise: In which year did Alexander Fleming discover penicillin? | 1892 | *1928 | 1982 | 1819
exercise: Toby's friend says Fleming saved everybody in like a day. Which is closer to the truth? | *Fleming noticed the mould in 1928, but it took many years, with Florey and Chain, to make penicillin a medicine | Fleming saved everybody in one day | Penicillin was invented by a dog | Fleming never found anything at all
exercise: In «Fleming noticed a mould on a dish», what kind of word is Fleming? | *A proper noun, the name of a person | An adjective, a describing word | A verb, an action word | The name of a place
test: Who wrote the James Bond spy stories? | Ernst Chain | Alexander Fleming | Howard Florey | *Ian Fleming
test: A Fleming can be a person from which place? | *Flanders, the Dutch-speaking north of Belgium | Penicillin land | Scotland | The bottom of a dish
exam: Which words in «Alexander Fleming noticed a mould killing germs» tell you who Fleming is? | killing germs | a mould | *Alexander Fleming, the first name and surname | noticed
